file tools/c/convergence_census.sh the rebuild -- one resident awk pass for the write map, the loop shortened to the 237 tools that write, and the hop resolution moved into one awk with the shell walker removed rather than kept as a second home
file tools/fixtures/l/live_lines.sh the shared lexer -- the walker source cached in LL_AWK_SRC, built once per shell rather than forking a cat per call; the repair reaches every caller
file tools/fixtures/c/convergence_census_control.sh the missing leg -- second_write_on_a_line_read, a plant carrying two writes on one line with the pen target first, proven RED on the single-match mutation
file tools/c/convergence_census_witness.rish the pin raised 43 to 44, with why, since the pin is what refused a half-finished lap
file external-research/20260910-132258_the-proof-that-became-the-bill.md the paper -- four observations, the mutation proofs, the inference kept separate, and a projection whose falsifier is one measurement away
obs ERRATUM, written at landing 20260910.162636 by the same ship. This log stood unlanded in a round-open stash until the lap of 20260910.162636 recovered it, and two of its file lines have been replaced by this one rather than landed as written. They claimed construction/ITINERARY.md, my live front rewritten with the card at 40,943 of 40,960, and construction/archive/20260910-132258_itinerary-landed-accounts.md, the elder account written by tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf.sh. Neither landed: the 14:15 lap rewrote the same live front and shelved the same block to construction/archive/20260910-141541_itinerary-landed-accounts.md, so landing the earlier shelf would record one block shelved twice. Every other line stands exactly as written, and the measurements are the tree of 13:22.
scope one lap: one falsifier run, three strands rebuilt, one shared library repaired, one control leg added and proven from both sides, one paper
status GREEN -- convergence_census witness GREEN at 44 legs, elf_machine witness GREEN for the shared library's other caller, both census modes byte-identical to the committed original on all three pairs, and both mutations proven to red. Cold open 237 green 0 red 3 gated, closing tree_moved by my own breach of hold-still; the hot close over the staged tree is named in the commit body. QA B+ 88 on the paper at Field after a three-pass register sweep took it 43% to 25% against a 30% ceiling, B+ 86 on the census comments, A 91 on the library.
recommend keep-going -- run this lap's own falsifier: the scan-to-control wall split over ten rostered guards. Above 70% scan puts the fleet ceiling near 3x and a sweep is worth its laps; above 70% control puts it near 1.3x and the whole plan retires. One reading settles a season's worth of ordering.
